# Infra and state locality

Prefer self-contained, per-repo solutions over machine-global or shared state.

When designing infra (test concurrency, locks, caches, coordination), do **not**
introduce folders or state that live outside the repo or are shared across
clones. Cap resources per-repo with a static knob instead.

Multiple clones of a repo are already independent, so cross-repo parallelism is
effectively free — favor a small per-repo cap over a shared coordinator. This is
why the simulator concurrency control is the per-repo `SRB_SIM_MAX` knob (see
`AGENTS.md > Build and test`) rather than a machine-wide semaphore in a shared
cache directory.
